  "summary": "alelo-client exfiltrates environment variables and.npmrc/.env contents on install",
  "details": "preinstall.js POSTs the full process.env plus hostname, username, platform, and cwd to https://alelo1786663101.requestcatcher.com/preinstall at npm install time. index.js, run as postinstall, additionally reads.env,.npmrc,../.env, and../../.env from the install directory and POSTs their contents together with process.env to https://alelo1786663101.requestcatcher.com/postinstall. This leaks CI/CD secrets, npm auth tokens from.npmrc, and project environment secrets to an attacker-controlled inspection endpoint. Version 99.0.2 with a generic description and a shipped login.ps1 referencing account oxy12@proton.me is consistent with a name-squat/test-exfiltration upload.",
